         <div type="bio">
            <p>British poet, critic, and editor. Symons had been introduced to Joyce by <name type="person" key="yeat65">W. B. Yeats</name>, after which Symons corresponded with Joyce about his collection of poems, <name type="work">Chamber Music</name>. In October 1906 Symons recommended the book to <name type="person" key="math51">Elkin Mathews</name>, who published it in May 1907. Symons and Joyce corresponded sporadically through the early 1930s, and Symons contributed the “Epilogue” to <name type="work">The Joyce Book</name>, edited by <name type="person" key="hugh82">Herbert Hughes</name> (London: Sylvan Press and Humphrey Milford Oxford University Press, 1933). <hi rend="bold">Dirk Van Hulle</hi> and <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
